          %h2#informal_definition Informal definition
          %p
            Toda-Smith complexes are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+spectra"} finite spectra
            characterized by having a particularly simple homology, and are used in stable homotopy theory.
          %p
            Toda-Smith complexes provided examples of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+map"} periodic map
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                nilpotent and periodicity theorems
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/nilpotent+and+periodicity+theorems"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
            (localized at a prime) into families of maps via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
          %h2#mathematical_context Mathematical Context
          %p
            The story begins with the degree p map on
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            (as a circle in the complex plane):
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \to S^1
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi z
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto z^p
          %p
            The degree p map is well defined for
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^k
            in general, where
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi math
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in math{N}
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^{\infty}S^1 \to \Sigma^{\infty}S^1 =: \mathbb{S}^1 \to \mathbb{S}^1
            and we take the cofiber of the resulting map:
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \xrightarrow{p} S \to S/p
          %p
            We find that
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/p
            has the remarkable property of coming from a Moore space (i.e., a designer (co)homology space:
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(X) \simeq Z/p
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{H}^*(X)
            is trivial for all
            = succeed ")." do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \neq n
          %h2#formal_definition Formal definition
          %p
            The
            = succeed "th" do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(n)
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \{-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, ... \}
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mtext :=
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi BP
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_*(V(n)) \text{:=} [\mathbb{S}^0, BP \wedge V(n)]
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_*/(p, ..., v_n)
          %p
            That is, Toda-Smith complexes are completely characterized by their
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(n)
            satisfying one of the following equations:
          %ul
            %li
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_*(V(-1)) \simeq BP_*
            %li
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_*(V(0)) \simeq BP_*/p
            %li
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_*(V(1)) \simeq BP_*/(p, v_1)
            %li etc.
          %h2#examples_of_todasmith_complexes Examples of Toda-Smith complexes
          %ul
            %li
              the sphere spectrum,
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi BP
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi BP
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_*(S^0) \simeq BP_*
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(-1)
            %li
              the mod p Moore spectrum,
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi BP
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi BP
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_*(S/p) \simeq BP_*/p
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(0)
          %h2#relevance_to_stable_homotopy_theory Relevance to stable homotopy theory
          %p
            It may help the reader to recall that that
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi BP
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP_* = \mathbb{Z}_p[v_1, v_2, ...]
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |v_i| = 2(p^i-1)
          %p
            The periodic maps,
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mi t
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_t, \beta_t,
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_t
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(0)_k, V(1)_k,
            and
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(2)_k
            respectively.
          %p
            (… add in their relation to the
            %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_2
            periodic elements, and the reasoning behind the shift
            = succeed ")" do
              %math#mathml_f1e4d471e4702506a62e19022ec39779b7d32702_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2(p^i-1)
